{# ABOUT, seam variant (theme.components.about = 'about_seam'; needs
   theme.style.seam set, or the clip ids resolve to nothing and the panel
   renders as a plain rectangle over the photograph).

   From xl the photograph is the section's ground and a tinted panel is laid
   over the left 58% of it, its right edge cut with the seam curve. Below xl
   the split turns horizontal: photograph on top, panel below, the horizontal
   seam along the bottom of the photograph.

   THE SPLIT STARTS AT xl, NOT lg. 1024-1279 is the iPad-landscape band and
   gets the stacked arrangement; a photograph beside a column is a layout, a
   photograph beside a narrow gutter of type is not.

   The clips are Tailwind arbitrary properties so the responsive selectors
   are generated — a hand-written compound selector in styles.scss may not
   survive the postcss chain.

   THE PHOTOGRAPH HAS TO CARRY ITS SUBJECT IN ITS RIGHT HALF. The panel
   covers the left 58% of the viewport, and object-position X is inert on a
   frame narrower than its box, so pick a room frame with the subject right
   of centre — a centred portrait gets the panel edge down the middle of the
   face. Vertical: object-cover on a portrait in a landscape band chooses a
   ~46% band of the picture; set the Y position to put the
   subject in it (an arbitrary object-position value on the img).

   Pair it with menus_schedule directly beneath: the photo column there is
   sized so the two seams meet at the section break (seam-defs.njk). On its
   own it sits on secondary-50, so re-derive the ground alternation — the
   stock menus band is secondary-50 too. #}
<section id="about" class="relative isolate overflow-hidden bg-secondary-50">
  <img
    src="{{ client.about.image }}"
    alt="{{ client.about.imageAlt or client.name }}"
    loading="lazy"
    decoding="async"
    sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 74vw, 100vw"
    class="h-[22rem] w-full object-cover [clip-path:url(#seam-h)] sm:h-[30rem] xl:absolute xl:inset-y-0 xl:left-auto xl:right-0 xl:h-full xl:w-[74%] xl:[clip-path:none]"
  />

  {# The panel does the vertical centring (min-height + items-center); an
     inner h-full against a min-height parent computes to auto and centres
     nothing. Its left padding is the site wrapper's own text edge, so the
     copy lines up with every other section. #}
  <div class="relative w-full bg-secondary-50 xl:flex xl:min-h-[46rem] xl:w-[58%] xl:items-center xl:[clip-path:url(#seam-v-out)]">
    <div class="container-site py-16 sm:py-20 xl:w-full xl:max-w-none xl:px-0 xl:py-24 xl:pl-[calc(max((100vw-80rem)/2,0px)+2rem)] xl:pr-[20%]">
      {# Centred while stacked (a full-width band, the same shape as every
         .section-head), left once it sits inside the off-centre panel. #}
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center xl:mx-0 xl:max-w-xl xl:text-left" data-reveal="up">
        {% if client.about.eyebrow %}<p class="eyebrow">{{ client.about.eyebrow }}</p>{% endif %}
        <h2 class="section-title !mt-0 xl:after:mx-0">{{ client.about_title }}</h2>
        <p class="mt-6 text-pretty text-lg/8 text-gray-700">{{ client.about_desc_one }}</p>
        <div class="mt-5 space-y-5 text-pretty text-lg/8 text-gray-600">
          <p>{{ client.about_desc_two }}</p>
          <p>{{ client.about_desc_three }}</p>
        </div>
        {# Optional sign-off (client.about.tagline): letterspaced in the
           accent above a short hairline that stops at the text. #}
        {%- if client.about.tagline %}
        <p class="mt-9 inline-block border-t border-accent-400 pt-4 font-display text-base font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.24em] text-accent-700">{{ client.about.tagline }}</p>
        {%- endif %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
